<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tedorigawa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1577</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tedorigawa was fought in 1577 at the Tedori River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaga-province">Kaga Province</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, between the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Uesugi Kenshin</a> and an army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shibata-katsuie">Shibata Katsuie</a>. Kenshin's troops routed the Oda army as it crossed the river. Kenshin died the following spring before he could follow up his victory, and the Oda soon recovered the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tedorigawa.jpg" alt="Battle of Tedorigawa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: クハ４１９－５ · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%89%8B%E5%8F%96%E5%B7%9D_%E5%B7%9D%E5%8C%97%E5%A4%A7%E6%A9%8B%E3%82%88%E3%82%8A%E9%B6%B4%E6%9D%A5%E5%81%B4_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
